  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 119.0,
  "event_seq": 266,
  "root_problem": "CRM dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from a ~600/month baseline (Jun-Jul 2026) to 1180 (Aug) and 1260 (Sep) 2026 (E-04). Of disputed bills, 1240 (41%) carry an ESTIMATED read type (E-01); E-12 shows 1184 of these (95%) had a valid, timely AMI read exported to billing but rejected at import with status REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION, not a missing/lost read. E-13 shows validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01, compares the raw cumulative register value directly against 12-month m3 consumption history with no unit scaling, and E-14 shows firmware v4.2 meters (rolled out 2026-06) record registers in units of 0.1 m3 versus legacy plain m3 — a 10x magnitude mismatch that would cause BV-17's unscaled comparison to misflag normal v4.2 usage as high-consumption, forcing estimate substitution. This billing-import rule defect explains the mechanism producing most ESTIMATED-read disputed bills; it does not establish the cause of the ACTUAL-read majority (59%, 1785 bills) of disputes, which remains unattributed."
 },
